{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head e9a1c55a7690aabf88543c5159faae8a01e47f8b, artifact 743a2a496775310a8c4de63e6b7555aef461d36c.\n\nTwo blockers.\n\n1. This head deliberately has no durable implementation request or promise. Commit e9a1c55a carries Rests-On 9775ac1d, which is an assert, and artifact 743a2a49 directly rests only on that assert. AGENTS.md is explicit that work begins with a request and promise, every implementing commit rests on the request, and an assert is not a substitute. The review request's statement that the artifact and review are the whole filing therefore describes a process violation, not an exception. This cannot be repaired only by refiling the artifact: create the scoped request, claim it, carry the change in a new commit with the canonical request trailer, record the new artifact and readiness report, then request fresh exact-head review.\n\n2. The internal/app choice is no longer true in the world where this head would merge. The commit and artifact justify 72e8adfd because ca1decfc/83e60c30 was not in main. Exact approved head 83e60c30 has since merged as main commit 63d8d765, with stable current internal/app artifact 845e3cc9af4e2a888ceece1a72d5b31d9ba72fe1. The candidate's own rule chooses the later in-main artifact when both candidates are in main, as it does for cmd/gs. Carry onto current main and re-anchor deploy-a-resident.md and serve.md to 845e3cc9, or state and prove a different behavior-specific selection rule consistently. Landing the current rationale would make its central factual premise false immediately.\n\nThe other judgements are favorable. Replacing a retired anchor is a real defect because later succession cannot flare it again. b7c2ffe5 and 5644516f are live, non-stale, in-main replacements for the cmd/gs anchors. The wider docs artifact path is the repository's declared winner over the four page-level paths; those narrower artifacts should be retired in the eventual merge step. An anchor-only scope is acceptable here provided the carried head verifies that the unchanged prose still describes behavior present in the selected artifact commits; a wholesale prose rewrite is not required.\n\nArchitecture: only documentation provenance and the docs projection contract are affected. No kernel, Workroom fold, durable protocol, connector, or UI contract changes; architecture.md need not move.\n\nSecurity: repairing retired anchors improves warning integrity for operational and review documentation. No credentials or runtime authorization surface changes. The stale implementation basis is itself a supply-chain/process-integrity blocker, hence the requested new request-bound head.\n\nSimplification: the candidate correctly identifies the simplest preventive follow-up—make the docset anchor gate reject retired artifacts so future repairs are detected mechanically. That belongs in its own request and does not need to expand this head. The wider docs artifact also avoids four competing page-level successors.\n\nVerified at the exact head: make docs passed (including executable examples); git diff --check passed; the worktree is clean; and merge-tree against current main succeeds. These passing content gates do not cure the two provenance/currentness blockers.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:743a2a496775310a8c4de63e6b7555aef461d36c","head":"e9a1c55a7690aabf88543c5159faae8a01e47f8b","verdict":"changes-requested"}}